      "quoted_tweet_id": null,
      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "🚨 Aircraft Targeted TWICE by Laser in St. Paul—Lives Put at Risk! 🚨\n\nOn January 24, while supporting Operation Metro Surge, an ASTAR crew was targeted twice with a green laser from a residence in St Paul, MN. The suspect was observed lasering the aircraft from his back patio. The laser was directed into the cabin and into the eyes of the crew, creating a dangerous situation for everyone on board. \n\nLasering an aircraft is NOT a prank—it’s a federal crime.  Individuals caught shining lasers at aircraft can face serious consequences, including: \n \n🔴 Fines up to $11,000 per violation from the FAA  🔴 Criminal charges that can lead to up to 5 years in prison  🔴 Additional fines up to $250,000 under federal law \n \nLaser strikes can temporarily blind or distract pilots, risking the safety of the crew, passengers, and people on the ground. Law enforcement and aviation authorities are actively investigating and will pursue legal action against offenders. \n \nIf you witness laser activity targeting aircraft, report it immediately. Help us keep our skies safe!  #ReportLaserIncidents",
      "text_resolved": "🚨 Aircraft Targeted TWICE by Laser in St. Paul—Lives Put at Risk! 🚨\n\nOn January 24, while supporting Operation Metro Surge, an ASTAR crew was targeted twice with a green laser from a residence in St Paul, MN. The suspect was observed lasering the aircraft from his back patio. The laser was directed into the cabin and into the eyes of the crew, creating a dangerous situation for everyone on board. \n\nLasering an aircraft is NOT a prank—it’s a federal crime.  Individuals caught shining lasers at aircraft can face serious consequences, including: \n \n🔴 Fines up to $11,000 per violation from the FAA  🔴 Criminal charges that can lead to up to 5 years in prison  🔴 Additional fines up to $250,000 under federal law \n \nLaser strikes can temporarily blind or distract pilots, risking the safety of the crew, passengers, and people on the ground. Law enforcement and aviation authorities are actively investigating and will pursue legal action against offenders. \n \nIf you witness laser activity targeting aircraft, report it immediately. Help us keep our skies safe!  #ReportLaserIncidents",
